SAMANVAYA v0.1 — provenance, attribution, status
Date: 2026-11-23

SAMANVAYA is developed as a new architecture building on previous HUAP work:
https://github.com/Mircus/HUAP
HUAP original licensing: MIT, copyright (c) 2025 HUAP Team.

Repository reviewed: HUAP main, tree SHA
41f8548c9b6c38814bf4634df44b4f92748304b0

Retained at the level of design: JSONL tracing, semantic trace diff,
side-effect-free replay, explicit contracts, CLI testability, framework-neutral
instrumentation, bounded tool capabilities and human review gates.

Fresh in this baseline: five-pillar constitutional policy, typed mandates,
restricted delegation, revocation, collective hyperedges and quorum, action
purpose, fail-closed decision statuses, and governance test cases.

No HUAP source modules are vendored verbatim in this baseline. The compatibility
reader consumes HUAP v0.1 JSONL as untrusted historical data only. The new
trace schema is intentionally distinct: samanvaya.audit.v0.1.

Philosophical inspirations: Sanskrit terms Ṛta, Dharma, Adhikāra,
Samanvaya, Punarnavīkaraṇa and Lokasaṃgraha; technical interpretation is
independent of scripture. The 12-law mapping is a provisional interpretation
of the public series by Srinivas Gutta, not a reproduction or endorsement.
